.TH GOLARM 1 "2026" "golarm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
golarm \- terminal clock, timer, stopwatch & alarm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B golarm
.RB [ clock ]
.RB [ \-12 ]
.RB [ \-\-fa ]
.RB [ \-\-analog [=ansi] ]
.RB [ \-\-dial " design" ]
.RB [ \-\-dial\-only ]
.RB [ \-\-accent " #RRGGBB" ]
.RB [ \-\-calendar
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR name ]
.br
.B golarm timer
.I duration
.RB [ \-l
.IR label ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.br
.B golarm chrono
.br
.B golarm alarm
.I HH:MM
.RB [ \-l
.IR label ]
.br
.B golarm
.BR \-v " | " \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B golarm
is a terminal TUI combining a live clock with a choice of calendars,
a countdown timer, a lap stopwatch, and wall-clock alarms.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clock
Live clock (default command). Shows an optional analog dial, the Gregorian
date by default, and a day-progress bar.
.TP
.BI timer " duration"
Countdown timer with a compact display for narrow panes.
.I duration
accepts Go syntax (\fB90s\fR, \fB5m\fR, \fB1h30m\fR), bare seconds
(\fB90\fR), and colon forms (\fB10:00\fR = mm:ss, \fB1:30:00\fR).
.TP
.B chrono
Stopwatch with lap support.
.TP
.BI alarm " HH:MM"
Alarm at the next occurrence of a local time (24-hour, or with an am/pm suffix
such as \fB7:30pm\fR). Keep Golarm running until the alarm fires.
Adjust the target to a future time with \fB+\fR or \fB-\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-12 ", " \-\-12h
12-hour clock.
.TP
.BR \-fa ", " \-\-fa
Persian (Eastern Arabic) digits on the small text lines. Kitty uses thin
spaces to keep the digits in order. Very narrow panes use ASCII time if the
spaced digits cannot fit.
.TP
.BR \-\-analog "[=ansi]"
Open the analog clock. Golarm uses Kitty graphics when the terminal supports
them and draws the dial with color cells elsewhere. Append
.B =ansi
to force the color-cell dial.
.TP
.BI \-\-dial " design"
Open the analog clock with the classic, sector, or minimal dial.
Combine with \fB\-\-analog=ansi\fR to use color cells.
.TP
.B \-\-dial\-only
Open a centered analog dial. Shows compact time if the dial cannot fit.
.TP
.BI \-\-accent " #RRGGBB"
Set a fixed clock accent. Quote the color in the shell.
.TP
.BI \-\-calendar " mode"
Clock date display. Choose \fBgregorian\fR (default), \fBshamsi\fR, or
\fBboth\fR. This flag overrides \fBGOLARM_CALENDAR\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Color theme: \fBdefault\fR, \fBcatppuccin\fR, \fBgruvbox\fR,
\fBtokyo-night\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-label " text"
Label shown in the timer UI and its notification (timer and alarm).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Run a headless timer. Exit 0 when the countdown completes and attempt a
desktop notification. An interrupted countdown exits nonzero.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GOLARM_12H=1
Default to the 12-hour clock.
.TP
.B GOLARM_FA=1
Default to Persian digits.
.TP
.B GOLARM_CALENDAR=<mode>
Default date display for the clock (\fBgregorian\fR, \fBshamsi\fR, or \fBboth\fR).
.TP
.B GOLARM_THEME=<name>
Default theme.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B space
Pause or resume the countdown timer or stopwatch. Dismiss a fired alert.
.TP
.B r
Restart the timer, re-arm the alarm for the next occurrence of the displayed
time, or reset the stopwatch.
.TP
.B l
Record a lap (chrono).
.TP
.B a
Switch between analog and digital faces (clock).
.TP
.B f
Cycle the analog dial designs.
.TP
.B d
Toggle the dial-only view.
.TP
.B + ", " \- ", " "left", " "right"
Adjust the countdown or alarm time by one minute.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.SH FILES
Desktop notifications use
.BR notify-send (1)
and are best effort. They require a desktop notification daemon.
